<title>FRANCE: Esso confirms French refinery go-slow.</title>
<headline>Esso confirms French refinery go-slow.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Esso confirmed on Friday that its 150,000 barrels per day (bpd) Port Jerome refinery near Le Havre was running at a slow pace because of workers' disruptions.</p>
<p>A company spokesman said disruption started on Wednesday evening and would last until Saturday at 1300 GMT.</p>
<p>On Thursday the CFDT union said unspecified action was planned at Port Jerome.</p>
<p>The spokesman said he was not aware of any disruption at Esso's other refinery at Fos in southern France.</p>
<p>&quot;At this stage I have no information regarding Fos,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for Mobil confirmed the 70,000 bpd Gravenchon refinery in northern France was also hit by a go-slow.</p>
<p>Disruptions began on Wednesday and are expected to run until Friday at 1300 GMT.</p>
<p>The disruptions are over oil industry plans to cut some 1,500 refinery jobs over the next year to deal with overcapacity.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 543</p>
